\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CTF-GS{} framework. The method stores one compact foundation-feature Gaussian map with per-Gaussian codes, spatial context, and quality/visibility heads, then decodes it through shared global readout heads. The same map supports rendered dense feature maps for LERF 2D open-vocabulary grounding, compact primitive scores with a support-calibrated primitive readout for LERF direct 3D object selection, and direct point features for ScanNet queries. Frozen RADIO/SigLIP2/DINOv3/SAM3 heads, multiview-registration-to-field support distillation, and geometry/visibility losses are training constraints; the main compact direct readout does not require a multiview-registration feature cache or an official RGB SAM decoder.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{3}{\method {} framework. The method stores one compact foundation-feature Gaussian map with per-Gaussian codes, spatial context, and quality/visibility heads, then decodes it through shared global readout heads. The same map supports rendered dense feature maps for LERF 2D open-vocabulary grounding, compact primitive scores with a support-calibrated primitive readout for LERF direct 3D object selection, and direct point features for ScanNet queries. Frozen RADIO/SigLIP2/DINOv3/SAM3 heads, multiview-registration-to-field support distillation, and geometry/visibility losses are training constraints; the main compact direct readout does not require a multiview-registration feature cache or an official RGB SAM decoder}{figure.1}{}}
